"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[8658],{88658:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"schemaVersion":1,"locale":"en","slug":"10-vychety","title":"Lesson 10. Tax deductions: Money the state returns if you ask","sourceFingerprint":"4729302deaabf2e02aa87906fe4cd9c353ec21ba06e112dcf4f2e2cc16548a53","blocks":[{"id":"b001","markdown":"## Tax deductions"},{"id":"b002","markdown":"Money the state returns if you ask"},{"id":"b003","markdown":"If formally employed, tax is withheld from salary every month. Your employer handles it, so almost nobody notices."},{"id":"b004","markdown":"In several cases the state returns part: healthcare, education, sport, buying housing, long-term savings and children. Many have heard this but imagine piles of paperwork and queues. In reality, almost everything can be done online, and refunds range from thousands to hundreds of thousands of rubles."},{"id":"b005","markdown":"### How it works"},{"id":"b006","markdown":"A tax deduction reduces the income on which tax is calculated."},{"id":"b007","markdown":"For example, annual income of 900 000 RUB taxed at 13% means 117 000 RUB paid. Then you spend 100 000 RUB on dentistry. Recalculated taxable income is 800 000 RUB and tax 104 000 RUB. The 13 000 RUB overpayment can be refunded."},{"id":"b008","markdown":"This implies 3 rules."},{"id":"b009","markdown":"- You can recover only tax actually paid. Without formal taxable salary, there is nothing to refund."},{"id":"b010","markdown":"- Refunds use your rate. Since 2025, tax has been progressive: 13% up to 2.4 million RUB annually, 15% on the portion from 2.4 to 5 million RUB, then 18%, 20% and 22%. If you pay 15%, the refund uses 15%."},{"id":"b011","markdown":"- Claims cover the last 3 years. In 2026 that means expenses from 2023, 2024 and 2025."},{"id":"b012","markdown":"Self-employed people paying professional-income tax and sole traders under simplified or patent regimes cannot claim without other personal-income-taxable income. Nor can non-working people without taxable income or tax non-residents, meaning those present in Russia for fewer than 183 days annually."},{"id":"b013","markdown":"A detail from lesson 6: deductions do not offset tax on deposit interest, which is a separate tax base."},{"id":"b014","markdown":"DEDUCTION REDUCES TAXABLE INCOME. INCOME 900 000 RUB, TAX 117 000 RUB. INCOME 800 000 RUB, TAX 104 000 RUB. DENTISTRY COST 100 000 RUB: REFUND 13 000 RUB."},{"id":"b015","markdown":"### Healthcare, education and sport"},{"id":"b016","markdown":"Healthcare covers doctors, tests, dentistry, prescribed medicine and voluntary medical insurance. It can include yourself, spouse, parents and children below 18, or below 24 in full-time education. The clinic needs a licence and supplies a tax-purpose medical-payment certificate. Many clinics already send data directly to the tax authority."},{"id":"b017","markdown":"Expensive treatment on the government list, such as complex surgery, is uncapped: tax is refunded against the full amount. Its certificate carries code 2. Education includes your own study in any format: university, courses, driving school or professional development; full-time study for children or siblings below 24; and a spouse. The institution must be licensed: ask directly."},{"id":"b018","markdown":"Sport includes fitness, swimming and clubs at organisations on the Sports Ministry list, published regionally. Since 2026, sport for retired parents can qualify if the contract and payment are in your name."},{"id":"b019","markdown":"Limits: healthcare, your own education and sport jointly allow 150 000 RUB of annual expenses, up to 19 500 RUB returned at 13%. Children’s education has a separate 110 000 RUB limit per child. Expensive qualifying treatment has no limit."},{"id":"b020","markdown":"Important: a social deduction does not carry forward. Paying several years of tuition upfront only uses one year’s cap; the rest is lost. Pay annually where possible."},{"id":"b021","markdown":"### Children"},{"id":"b022","markdown":"The standard monthly deduction reduces taxable salary by 1 400 RUB for the first child, 2 800 RUB for the second and 6 000 RUB for the third and each later child. It applies until cumulative salary since January exceeds 450 000 RUB, and each parent can qualify. Apply through payroll; if not receiving it, submit the request."},{"id":"b023","markdown":"A family tax payment began in 2026 for working parents with 2 or more children. Per-person family income must not exceed 1.5 times the regional subsistence minimum. The state then returns personal income tax paid above 6%. Other conditions apply, such as no child-support arrears. Each parent may receive it."},{"id":"b024","markdown":"Applications for the previous year run through Gosuslugi or the Social Fund from June 1 to October 1. The 2025 window has closed; the 2026 window opens June 1, 2027."},{"id":"b025","markdown":"### Housing"},{"id":"b026","markdown":"The largest deduction has 2 forms. Housing purchase expenses up to 2 million RUB can yield up to 260 000 RUB at 13%. If the property cost less, unused base may carry to another purchase. Paid mortgage interest up to 3 million RUB can yield up to 390 000 RUB. That interest deduction applies to one property only."},{"id":"b027","markdown":"Together this is up to 650 000 RUB, claimable gradually year after year until the limit is used. For a home bought in marriage, each spouse may have deduction rights."},{"id":"b028","markdown":"### GTO fitness standards"},{"id":"b029","markdown":"Since 2025, earning a GTO fitness badge provides an 18 000 RUB annual deduction, returning 2 340 RUB at 13%. Since 2026, a preventive medical examination suffices; a full screening is not required. The amount is modest, but if you already train, why not?"},{"id":"b030","markdown":"### Long-term savings"},{"id":"b031","markdown":"The state also refunds tax for long-term saving through third-type individual investment accounts, IIS-3, and long-term savings programmes with non-state pension funds. Contributions up to 400 000 RUB annually can yield up to 52 000 RUB at 13%. Since September 1, 2026, long-term life-insurance deductions share that same 400 000 RUB cap across all these instruments."},{"id":"b032","markdown":"Holding-period conditions apply. For example, an IIS-3 opened in 2026 must remain open at least 5 years, otherwise deductions must be repaid. The next module covers this alongside investing."},{"id":"b033","markdown":"How much will the state return?"},{"id":"b034","markdown":"Healthcare, education and sport. Child education. Housing purchase. Mortgage interest. Expenses: 100 000 RUB. Formal annual income: 900 000 RUB. Refund: 13 000 RUB."},{"id":"b035","markdown":"Refund: 100 000 RUB \xd7 13%. Shared annual expense cap 150 000 RUB, with no carry-forward."},{"id":"b036","markdown":"Check your taxpayer account: a prefilled application may already be waiting. The 15% rate applies to income above 2.4 million RUB yearly; this source example simplifies by applying it to the whole amount."},{"id":"b037","markdown":"### How to receive the money"},{"id":"b038","markdown":"Simplified applications through the taxpayer account or Gosuslugi apply to expenses from 2024. Many clinics, universities, sports clubs and banks send data directly, enabling prefilled applications. Check and sign in your taxpayer account. Review usually takes up to a month and money arrives in your account. Often an application is already waiting unnoticed."},{"id":"b039","markdown":"Through a banking app. Some large banks, including Sber and T-Bank, arrange social deductions in-app if you paid a participating organisation. The bank prepares the application and you sign."},{"id":"b040","markdown":"Through your employer, without waiting for year-end. Ask the tax authority to confirm eligibility. Around a month later it notifies the employer; payroll stops withholding tax until the deduction is used. Take-home pay rises for several months."},{"id":"b041","markdown":"Independently, through a 3-NDFL return. Slower but universal, suitable for any deduction and any of the 3 years. Complete it in your taxpayer account and attach contract, payment certificates or receipts and licence scans. Review takes up to 3 months, followed by up to another month for payment."},{"id":"b042","markdown":"### What to do now"},{"id":"b043","markdown":"- Open your taxpayer account and check for prefilled applications."},{"id":"b044","markdown":"- Recall healthcare, dentistry, education, sport and housing expenses in 2023, 2024 and 2025. The 2023 deadline expires at the end of 2026."},{"id":"b045","markdown":"- Create a paper or cloud folder for contracts, receipts and certificates from 2026. It saves time in early 2027."},{"id":"b046","markdown":"- Check whether payroll applies your standard child deduction."},{"id":"b047","markdown":"### The essentials"},{"id":"b048","markdown":"- Deductions refund part of tax already paid, no more than paid, at your rate and for the last 3 years."},{"id":"b049","markdown":"- Healthcare, own education and sport: up to 150 000 RUB expenses yearly. Child education: up to 110 000 RUB per child. Expensive qualifying treatment is uncapped."},{"id":"b050","markdown":"- Housing: up to 2 million RUB purchase expenses and 3 million RUB mortgage interest."},{"id":"b051","markdown":"- The easiest start is a prefilled application in your taxpayer account."},{"id":"b052","markdown":"The module’s lessons end here. Next are 2 guides: the first 30 days, and interest-free card use for those it suits. The following module covers protecting savings and beginning to invest."}],"terms":[{"id":"iis","term":"Individual investment account (IIS)","definition":"An account with tax benefits. Type A refunds 13% of contributions, up to 52 000 RUB annually. Type B exempts profits from tax. Its three-year period begins when opened."},{"id":"ndfl","term":"Personal income tax (NDFL)","definition":"Personal income tax. This course’s educational calculations use 13% up to 2.4 million RUB of annual income and 15% for the next band. Since 2025 the main scale has been progressive; special rules apply to other types of income. Check current rates and deduction eligibility with the Federal Tax Service."},{"id":"prozhitochnyy-minimum","term":"Subsistence minimum","definition":"The monthly amount the state estimates a person needs for essentials. It determines benefit eligibility and is protected from debt collection. It is a survival threshold, not a comfortable living standard."},{"id":"oblako","term":"Cloud services","definition":"Renting someone else’s servers over the internet: a company pays for computing capacity used instead of building its own data centre. This is cheaper and faster, but its website or app depends on the provider’s infrastructure working."}],"quizzes":[{"id":"10-vychety-q1","q":"You spent 100 000 RUB on dentistry, your tax rate is 13% and annual tax paid is 90 000 RUB. What can be refunded?","options":["100 000 RUB","90 000 RUB","13 000 RUB"],"correct":2},{"id":"10-vychety-q2","q":"You are self-employed and pay only professional-income tax. Can you claim a social education deduction?","options":["Yes, always","No, unless you also have income subject to personal income tax","Yes, but only for children’s education"],"correct":1},{"id":"10-vychety-q3","q":"For which years can a healthcare deduction be claimed in 2026?","options":["2023, 2024 and 2025","Only 2025","Any year since starting work"],"correct":0}],"officialSources":[]}')}}]);